1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,136
Cent #2616.

2
00:00:02,508 --> 00:00:05,828
A penny struck in 1912, at Philadelphia.

3
00:00:06,408 --> 00:00:09,253
The only Cent from 1912 in the collection.

4
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:11,993
Its surface has turned red.

5
00:00:12,654 --> 00:00:13,525
Full Red.

6
00:00:14,442 --> 00:00:17,530
In the Traits Atlas, full means red dominates

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,501
the surface: a clearly red cent at first glance.

8
00:00:22,164 --> 00:00:24,207
Across Lincoln's head and shoulder,

9
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:25,914
grey-green films.

10
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:27,841
Significant Verdigris.

11
00:00:28,201 --> 00:00:29,942
Significant means a major visual

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,206
actor, but not yet fully dominant.

13
00:00:33,774 --> 00:00:35,667
71 Cents are Full Red.

14
00:00:36,247 --> 00:00:37,386
This is the oldest.

15
00:00:37,874 --> 00:00:40,381
The next is from 1957.

16
00:00:41,832 --> 00:00:44,259
Compare Cent #9540,

17
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:48,567
from 1911, whose only trait is Notable Obsidian.

18
00:00:49,518 --> 00:00:52,097
One year apart, a different surface.

19
00:00:53,537 --> 00:00:55,789
Scarcity written by survival.

20
00:00:56,603 --> 00:00:58,494
Among the 10,000 Cents,

21
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:01,502
the older the year, the fewer there are.

22
00:01:02,082 --> 00:01:04,742
12 years appear only once.

23
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,004
In the words of Martin Lehnen,

24
00:01:09,272 --> 00:01:12,418
in his essay "Reflections on Mint Years":

25
00:01:13,207 --> 00:01:15,947
"These CENTS are extraordinary anomalies

26
00:01:16,052 --> 00:01:17,677
with absolute scarcity:

27
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:23,156
…1912, and 1911 stand as singular relics."

28
00:01:24,769 --> 00:01:26,510
Coin collecting turned over.

29
00:01:27,207 --> 00:01:29,320
In the words of collector Dagmar:

30
00:01:29,646 --> 00:01:32,037
"Unlike traditional coin collectors,

31
00:01:32,061 --> 00:01:34,730
who prefer old coins in pristine condition,

32
00:01:35,171 --> 00:01:37,030
we “degens” value the symbolic

33
00:01:37,087 --> 00:01:39,072
decay of these fiat coins."
